      {
        "id": 126702,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-19T19:34:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>However, if guise was before scholar in turn order, at the start of Guide's turn the copied text would trigger, healing Guise and destroying uh, yeah I'm that guy. &nbsp;Because in this instance it is the copied text on Guise's card acting.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Just a clarification, it's not Guise being before The Scholar in turn order, but Uh, Yeah, I'm That Guy! being in play before Expect the Worst (unless Fixed Point is in play of course). Guise just gets more use out of the reducing damage to 0 if Guise's turn is before The Scholar.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:11.752Z",
